   408	      // diagnostics, WITHOUT serializing throughput. Every write below is issued as
   409	      // write(text, cb) and is NOT awaited per-chunk; the callback decrements a
   410	      // shared pending counter. drainPending() — awaited by the finally BEFORE the
   411	      // error listeners are removed — resolves once every in-flight write has
   412	      // settled, so a late EPIPE from the FINAL chunk(s) fires while our named
   413	      // 'error' listeners are still attached. This closes the residual window that
   414	      // F-020/F-023 left on fire-and-forget live passthrough writes.
   415	      let pendingWrites = 0;
   416	      let onDrained: (() => void) | null = null;
