{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"reasoning","text":"**Analyzing GC worktree cleanup issue**
**Identifying cross-host runtime cleanup bug**

I’ve found a maintainability issue where expired cross-host runs aren’t fully cleaned because GC tries to remove already deleted worktrees, causing git errors and making GC fail to reclaim them. The snapshot cleanup happens immediately after run completion, but later GC calls still try to remove vanished worktrees, which leads to retention bugs. I'll consider if tests cover this scenario."}}

